<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Guayaquil Conference</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1822</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guayaquil">Guayaquil</a> Conference was the meeting of the two leading liberators of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-america">South America</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simon-bolivar">Simón Bolívar</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jose-de-san-martin">José de San Martín</a>, at Guayaquil on 26 and 27 July 1822. Held in private, it left no reliable record, but soon afterwards San Martín withdrew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a> and public life, leaving Bolívar to complete the liberation of Peru.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/guayaquil-conference.jpg" alt="Guayaquil Conference" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Padaguan · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Detalle_del_Hemiciclo_de_la_Rotonda.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
